(3032441, 423658, 39057, '<td valign="top">You made the right choice.</td>', 'You made the right choice.', '2006-11-15 00:19:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3032448, 421498, 34659, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot.  Really gorgeous work.  Well done.</td>', 'Beautiful shot.  Really gorgeous work.  Well done.', '2006-11-15 00:19:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3032467, 422974, 39057, '<td valign="top">I like your concept here. Too bad for the dq.</td>', 'I like your concept here. Too bad for the dq.', '2006-11-15 00:21:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3032497, 424454, 6349, '<td valign="top">I think this is easily one of the top photos in the challenge composition wise and could have had a good chance at ribboning but the post processing in my opinion is taking away from the beautiful photo that you started with.</td>', 'I think this is easily one of the top photos in the challenge composition wise and could have had a good chance at ribboning but the post processing in my opinion is taking away from the beautiful photo that you started with.', '2006-11-15 00:24:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3032502, 424378, 31399, '<td valign="top">well durn, for me "reflection" would include using twins in setups (people AND/OR shoes :)  very sorry this didn''t score better.  Idea is cool and wonder if the blue were different color less voters would have thought it was a mirror???heck if I know...round these parts...WHO knows?lol</td>', 'well durn, for me "reflection" would include using twins in setups (people AND/OR shoes :)  very sorry this didn''t score better.  Idea is cool and wonder if the blue were different color less voters would have thought it was a mirror???heck if I know...round these parts...WHO knows?lol', '2006-11-15 00:24:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3032508, 421424, 36076, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by deepfrog17:</b></div><hr/><i> not enough reflection to make it significant element of your photo </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>this entire photo is about reflection. picture it without the sky in the windows. it is the blue in the glass that draws the entire composition together. seems to me there''s always at least one person who thinks they can find a reason why every photo doesn''t fit the challenge.</td>', 'Originally posted by deepfrog17: not enough reflection to make it significant element of your photo   this entire photo is about reflection. picture it without the sky in the windows. it is the blue in the glass that draws the entire composition together. seems to me there''s always at least one person who thinks they can find a reason why every photo doesn''t fit the challenge.', '2006-11-15 00:25:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3032509, 424292, 60862, '<td valign="top">So - why did this score .7 below your free study?  I''m guessing because it''s darker and because here you''re actually contrasting the two pieces instead of making the reflection blend in.  But I think it''s a great variation on the theme.</td>', 'So - why did this score .7 below your free study?  I''m guessing because it''s darker and because here you''re actually contrasting the two pieces instead of making the reflection blend in.  But I think it''s a great variation on the theme.', '2006-11-15 00:25:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3032517, 423252, 40718, '<td valign="top">''Grats Ursula!</td>', '''Grats Ursula!', '2006-11-15 00:25:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3032524, 421424, 36076, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by svstoltz:</b></div><hr/><i> In part it''s almost a cool geomeric abstract, but its also just the side of building.  Details like the projecting roofline, and patio umbrella detract from the simple powerful forms </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>while i agree that the umbrella is a bit distracting, the basic editing rules clearly state that cloning anything but bad pixels out is not allowed. as for the projecting roofline... i like it, but that''s a matter of personal opinion.</td>', 'Originally posted by svstoltz: In part it''s almost a cool geomeric abstract, but its also just the side of building.  Details like the projecting roofline, and patio umbrella detract from the simple powerful forms   while i agree that the umbrella is a bit distracting, the basic editing rules clearly state that cloning anything but bad pixels out is not allowed. as for the projecting roofline... i like it, but that''s a matter of personal opinion.', '2006-11-15 00:26:21.000000', NULL, 0),
