(3033315, 424244, 64209, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> How did you get a fall leaf to reflect green? Fantastic. And that large green shape on top completes composition. You have 3 main S curves reflecting each other, and a smaller S curve, also reflected. The S curve is a beautiful line. You can''t lose! 8 bump to 9 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you!  The green was already there - I merely increased green and yellow in the colour balance, and decreased red.  I felt that the green reflection was more important than the red colours in the leaf for this competition.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: How did you get a fall leaf to reflect green? Fantastic. And that large green shape on top completes composition. You have 3 main S curves reflecting each other, and a smaller S curve, also reflected. The S curve is a beautiful line. You can''t lose! 8 bump to 9   Thank you!  The green was already there - I merely increased green and yellow in the colour balance, and decreased red.  I felt that the green reflection was more important than the red colours in the leaf for this competition.', '2006-11-15 06:10:21.000000', NULL, 0),
