(3035891, 423870, 56658, '<td valign="top">i think it would have worked better for this challenge if you had cropped in to the red boat and its reflection.</td>', 'i think it would have worked better for this challenge if you had cropped in to the red boat and its reflection.', '2006-11-15 21:32:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3035895, 423230, 43031, '<td valign="top">Nice job Rick. Really sharp pic, and good reflection. You might re-think the composition though. Especially with reflections, it''s more impactful here if the top corner of the building were not cut off. I know, the pictures about the reflections, but it''s also about the symmetry involved in the reflected object. <br/> <br/>If only ideas: shoot closer to sunset, just as the last light hits the buildings, and use a graduated ND filter to balance the sky and land exposure values. Woulda beat me for sure, I''d think ;)</td>', 'Nice job Rick. Really sharp pic, and good reflection. You might re-think the composition though. Especially with reflections, it''s more impactful here if the top corner of the building were not cut off. I know, the pictures about the reflections, but it''s also about the symmetry involved in the reflected object.  If only ideas: shoot closer to sunset, just as the last light hits the buildings, and use a graduated ND filter to balance the sky and land exposure values. Woulda beat me for sure, I''d think ;)', '2006-11-15 21:33:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3036282, 424412, 66384, '<td valign="top">This is very interesting. Thanks for sharing the technique you used to create the ghost. I''m going to have to try it myself.<br/> <br/>P.S. She''s a cute girl!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-16 00:00:32.</i></td>', 'This is very interesting. Thanks for sharing the technique you used to create the ghost. I''m going to have to try it myself. P.S. She''s a cute girl!', '2006-11-15 23:57:39.000000', '2006-11-16 00:00:32.000000', 0),
(3036293, 423907, 16918, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tnun:</b></div><hr/><i> Ugh.  These are not flies. Are they reflected, or just lying on the surface? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m sorry. These are not flies, they are monkeys.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-16 00:54:02.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by tnun: Ugh.  These are not flies. Are they reflected, or just lying on the surface?   I''m sorry. These are not flies, they are monkeys.', '2006-11-16 00:00:02.000000', '2006-11-16 00:54:02.000000', 0),
(3036304, 423907, 16918, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by santiago9er:</b></div><hr/><i> So where''s the reflection? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Please open your eyes. There were also a few others asking the same question. <br/> <br/>This picture was taken in a shallow lake (about one foot deep) with bright granite bed. The dead flies were floating and their shadows, including the mineral bottle, were cast onto the bright granite bed. Can you see their reflection now? <br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-16 00:57:48.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by santiago9er: So where''s the reflection?   Please open your eyes. There were also a few others asking the same question.  This picture was taken in a shallow lake (about one foot deep) with bright granite bed. The dead flies were floating and their shadows, including the mineral bottle, were cast onto the bright granite bed. Can you see their reflection now?  ', '2006-11-16 00:02:06.000000', '2006-11-16 00:57:48.000000', 0),
(3036325, 423907, 16918, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nefir:</b></div><hr/><i> Very neat shot. Interesting perspective! Love the shadows at the bottom of the water. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You have a photograhic eye and the only positive comment so far. Perhaps only you understand my works. <br/> <br/>Regardless the majority of the negative comments (which I believed they yet to trained their eyes), I would consider this picture remains as one of my classic shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by Nefir: Very neat shot. Interesting perspective! Love the shadows at the bottom of the water.   You have a photograhic eye and the only positive comment so far. Perhaps only you understand my works.  Regardless the majority of the negative comments (which I believed they yet to trained their eyes), I would consider this picture remains as one of my classic shot.', '2006-11-16 00:06:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3036359, 424412, 22537, '<td valign="top">The shot looks cluttered and you are relying too much on the effect for points. Too many distractions and not enough thought put into the composition.  It almost appears as it is a snapshot and looky what showed up as a cool incidental bonus within the shot.  Not to say that it was not intentional but if it was, it is well concealed. I guess presentation is everything and this seems to fall short.  Soory, but you asked. Better luck next time.</td>', 'The shot looks cluttered and you are relying too much on the effect for points. Too many distractions and not enough thought put into the composition.  It almost appears as it is a snapshot and looky what showed up as a cool incidental bonus within the shot.  Not to say that it was not intentional but if it was, it is well concealed. I guess presentation is everything and this seems to fall short.  Soory, but you asked. Better luck next time.', '2006-11-16 00:13:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3036376, 424412, 42013, '<td valign="top">You have a nice diagonal of blue accross the frame from top left to bottom right. But, the brightness of the ribbon, and secondarily the BG of your daughters picture serve to distract from the challenge theme. There is little unity of objects in the frame, either in shape or placement. IMHO, in the context of the challenge, the reflection does not stand out as the subject. I see the girl''s picture as the primary subject with secondary feeling prompted by the ghost image. I didn''t vote in the challenge but seems like a 5 or maybe a 6 would have been my choice.</td>', 'You have a nice diagonal of blue accross the frame from top left to bottom right. But, the brightness of the ribbon, and secondarily the BG of your daughters picture serve to distract from the challenge theme. There is little unity of objects in the frame, either in shape or placement. IMHO, in the context of the challenge, the reflection does not stand out as the subject. I see the girl''s picture as the primary subject with secondary feeling prompted by the ghost image. I didn''t vote in the challenge but seems like a 5 or maybe a 6 would have been my choice.', '2006-11-16 00:16:36.000000', NULL, 0),
