(3048511, 424383, 45475, '<td valign="top">Haha! Awesome prediction Amy! :D But I wouldn''t call it pure crap. As Don says, it''s an amazing ripple effect. I think where this has let you down a bit though, is composition. Turning the camera slightly clockwise (or even rotating the canvas before crop), would have gotten rid of the distracting diagonal at top right, giving the image more balance too.<br/> <br/>Personally, I think the voters were a bit harsh on you. I would have placed this in the mid 5s at least as the reflection itself and contrast are really quite good.</td>', 'Haha! Awesome prediction Amy! :D But I wouldn''t call it pure crap. As Don says, it''s an amazing ripple effect. I think where this has let you down a bit though, is composition. Turning the camera slightly clockwise (or even rotating the canvas before crop), would have gotten rid of the distracting diagonal at top right, giving the image more balance too. Personally, I think the voters were a bit harsh on you. I would have placed this in the mid 5s at least as the reflection itself and contrast are really quite good.', '2006-11-20 17:21:23.000000', NULL, 0),
